cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Interaction-Structured Motion Retargeting for Multi-Party
  Humanoid–Object Interactions
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite Buwen Zhang, sole author of the original
  project code. Third-party code, data, models, and assets keep their own
  licenses. No project license, DOI, release date, or publication venue is
  declared. Do not add preferred-citation until the paper is published.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Buwen
    family-names: Zhang
abstract: >-
  Kinematic retargeting for two Unitree G1 humanoids. Join studies a coupled
  joint-contact objective (EXT-JC) with a documented smoothing repair on six
  CORE4D carry clips. Soccer is a single-sequence case study of independent
  event-conditioned inverse kinematics and a post-IK ball. Frozen v41 is a
  visual baseline, not EXT-JC. Soccer does not jointly optimize the two robots.
keywords:
  - humanoid retargeting
  - multi-party interaction
  - kinematic reference
